-- title:
--   Local subring at a rational place versus its localisation
-- statement:
--   Let $L \subseteq F$ be fields with $F$ an $L$-algebra, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $L$, let $N_0$ be a subring of $F$ that is a local ring, and let $C'$ be a subring of $L$ all of whose elements lie in $A$. Assume that every $g \in N_0$ can be written so that, for some $o \in C'$ whose image $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,L\,F(o)$ lies in $N_0$, the difference $g - o$ is a non-unit of $N_0$. Let $T$ be the subring of $F$ generated by $N_0$ together with the image of $A$ in $F$, and let $\mathfrak p \subseteq T$ be the ideal spanned by those elements of $T$ that equal a non-unit of $N_0$ together with those that equal the image of an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $L_x$ be a subring of $F$ whose members are exactly the $f \in F$ with $f c = b$ for some $b, c \in T$, $c \notin \mathfrak p$; thus $L_x$ realises the localisation $T_{\mathfrak p}$ inside $F$. Finally let $P$ be a place of $F$ over $L$, that is, a valuation subring $\mathcal O_P \neq F$ of $F$ containing the image of $L$ and being a principal ideal ring, and assume $P$ is rational, i.e. $L$ surjects onto the residue field of $\mathcal O_P$; write $f \mapsto f(P) \in L$ for the induced evaluation (the $L$-preimage of the residue of $f$ when $f \in \mathcal O_P$, and $0$ otherwise). The theorem asserts the equivalence of: (i) $N_0 \subseteq \mathcal O_P$ and $f(P)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ for every non-unit $f$ of $N_0$; and (ii) for every $f \in L_x$ one has $f \in \mathcal O_P$ and $f(P) \in A$, with $f(P)$ a unit of $A$ if and only if $f$ is invertible in $L_x$.
--
--   This is the localisation dictionary translating a condition imposed on the local subring $N_0$ at a rational place into the corresponding condition on the localisation $T_{\mathfrak p}$ of $T = A[N_0]$ read inside $F$, the latter being the form in which places are compared with points of a model. It is used in the construction and descent of semistable models of modular curves of full level, where $N_0$ encodes a local presentation at a node.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_forall_localSubring_iff_forall_localization.lean

